| c. 10,000 BC || || First human settlement of the archipelago begins on [[Harujima]] island with the arrival of the ''Harujima-Kaze culture'', semi-nomadic hunter-gatherers who thrive on abundant marine life of the northern coast.
|-
| c. 5,000 BC || || Climate stabilization allows permanent habitation of central islands. The ''Oita-Yagi horizon'' emerges with introduction of wet-field farming and livestock management by seafaring migrants from the Chalamdra region.
|-
| 2nd millennium BC || || The [[Atsu]] people, of Zong maritime and Darasian steppe origins, populate majority of Harujima and Yagikoshu before being displaced by continental invaders with superior bronze weaponry.
|-
| 695 BC || February 17 || Traditional founding date of the [[Mitoyagi Empire]] by the Toyama Emperor, who consolidates fragmented clans of North Central Yagikoshu into the province of Mito and adopts the title of Mikado.
|}

===Miyagi Empire===

{| class="wikitable" width="100%"
|-
! style="background-color: #CEDFF2; text-align: center;" | Year
! style="background-color: #CEDFF2; text-align: center;" | Date
